("FirstTimeMom-1x7qg84",None,"expecting_mother","third_trimester","others_said",["baby_shower","in_laws","what_to_buy","unwanted_advice"],"Keeps talking how everything is so expensive and friends should be giving me some of the stuff. If I don't have the carrier picked yet she starts saying that if we had the babyshower we would have it already.","30 weeks, first baby; sister-in-law pushing a shower the couple has refused many times.",None),
("FirstTimeMom-1x7qg84",None,"expecting_mother","third_trimester","pain",["baby_shower","in_laws","registry","boundaries"],"I did not make or share a list! She did it for me! Picked stuff she assumed was essential and proceeded to put together a list for my babyshower that I absolutely do not want!!","The sister-in-law planned a surprise shower and wrote a registry for her.",None),
("FirstTimeMom-1x7qg84","ph6rvhn","expecting_mother","third_trimester","others_said",["what_to_buy","in_laws","price_value"],"Stroller is bought, arriving in a few weeks (was sold out had to wait to be available again!) - she says it's too expensive and are similar ones that are cheaper.","Her sister-in-law comments on every purchase.",None),
("FirstTimeMom-1x7qg84","ph6rvhn","expecting_mother","third_trimester","pain",["in_laws","what_to_buy","boundaries"],"She tries to control everything we buy. I understand she had to save on a few choices but it's not my reality and I want to do things my way.","Same reply.",None),
("FirstTimeMom-1x7qg84","ph6rvhn","expecting_mother","third_trimester","others_said",["feeding","unwanted_advice","in_laws"],"We also questioned my decision to EP a few times, saying breastfeeding is cheaper and pratical I dont have to buy bottles etc... I'm over it really.","Same reply; she plans to exclusively pump.",None),
("pregnant-1x7s894",None,"expecting_mother","third_trimester","trigger_moment",["birth_prep","not_ready","work_in_pregnancy"],"I’m 32 weeks pregnant and I’ve not done any birth preparations what so ever- this pregnancy has gone incredibly quick and my life is very busy.","Title: 'Not prepared enough for a vaginal delivery'. 192 comments.",None),
("pregnant-1x7s894",None,"expecting_mother","third_trimester","others_said",["family_comments","own_mother","birth_prep"],"My mum and sister have both told me I’m not prepared enough go have a vaginal birth and this has worried me. Am I too unprepared for a vaginal birth? How exactly do I need to prepare for one?","Same post; the comment that started her worry.",None),
("pregnant-1x7s894",None,"expecting_mother","third_trimester","tried_failed",["birth_course","birth_prep","uk_nhs"],"We tried booking onto antenatal classes but they were all full up. I’ve not had the time or drive to actually bother preparing for birth because I just assumed the midwives would have it covered.","Same post.",None),
("pregnant-1x7s894",None,"expecting_mother","third_trimester","tried_failed",["birth_prep","social_media","birth_fear"],"I tried watching birthing videos and antenatal videos to educate myself on labour and they’re just nauseating and have put my off wanting a vaginal birth.","Same post; her attempt to self-educate.",None),
